heinha@oslonett.no (Hein Haraldsen) writes:


>I have noticed thath there is always a gnomish wizard in the minetown 
>temple. Is there any reason for this, or is it maybe a bug? I have also 
>noticed something similar at the medusa level (a gremlin and a titan at 
>the beginning). 

There are two medusa levels. The one with her castle in the middle has
some monsters that are always generated: five ; / two S / one @ (ma'am
herself, asleep) / ten random monsters, and if random monsters are
generated later, they are always ;, S or g.

The other Medusa level has (to start with): six electric eels, Medusa
(asleep), one gremlin, one titan, four stone golems (asleep), two
cobras (asleep), an A, a yellow light (asleep), and 13 random monsters.
If random monsters are generated later, they are always ;, S or g.

The mines' town has: four watchmen, one watch captain, some shopkeepers
(number varies), and a priest(ess), all peaceful, plus six gnomes in
various rooms (two out of towm), two gnomish wizards in the temple, one
gnome lord in town, and one dwarf out of town. New monsters are
generated completely random.

Just for the heck of it, these are the monster that appear on the
Mines' Bottom level: One gnome king, three gnome lords, 2 gnomish
wizards, nine gnomes, two hobbits, three dwarves, and one other
randomly picked "h". This could be the occasional bugbear or mind
flayer. The stones that are generated are (in that order, all on the
same spot): a diamond, a random stone or gem, a diamond, a random stone
or gem, an emerald, a random stone or gem, an emerald, a random stone
or gem, an emerald, a random stone or gem, a ruby, a random stone or
gem, a ruby, an amethyst, a random stone or gem, an amethyst, and a
luckstone. Also, 7 other stones or gems are randomly generated on the
floor.

>Also, I would like to know what the watchmen are doing on the minetown 
>level, except for being annoying.

Nothing. They are keeping watch. They are always on the lookout for
people that abuse their hospitality, by quaffing uninvitedly form
fountains, or kicking open doors.

